JSON format

1) Set or replace one object

POST /api/object

Text

{
  "screen": 0,
  "slot": 0,
  "object": {
    "type": "text",
    "visible": true,
    "x": 1,
    "y": 10,
    "r": 255,
    "g": 255,
    "b": 0,
    "text": "HELLO",
    "size": 1
  }
}

Rectangle

{
  "screen": 0,
  "slot": 1,
  "object": {
    "type": "rect",
    "visible": true,
    "x": 2,
    "y": 2,
    "w": 20,
    "h": 10,
    "filled": false,
    "r": 0,
    "g": 255,
    "b": 0
  }
}

Circle

{
  "screen": 0,
  "slot": 2,
  "object": {
    "type": "circle",
    "visible": true,
    "x": 32,
    "y": 16,
    "radius": 6,
    "filled": true,
    "r": 0,
    "g": 0,
    "b": 255
  }
}

Line

{
  "screen": 0,
  "slot": 3,
  "object": {
    "type": "line",
    "visible": true,
    "x1": 0,
    "y1": 0,
    "x2": 63,
    "y2": 31,
    "r": 255,
    "g": 0,
    "b": 0
  }
}

5) Clear one object

POST /api/clearObject

{
  "screen": 0,
  "slot": 0
}


6) Clear one whole screen

POST /api/clearScreen

{
  "screen": 0
}


7) Optionally switch active screen from HTTP

POST /api/showScreen

{
  "screen": 5
}


8) Query status

GET /api/status



Example

Put text on screen 0 slot 0

curl -X POST http://192.168.1.228/api/object \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "screen":0,
    "slot":0,
    "object":{
      "type":"text",
      "visible":true,
      "x":1,
      "y":8,
      "r":255,
      "g":255,
      "b":0,
      "text":"HELLO",
      "size":1
    }
  }'

Clear screen 0

curl -X POST http://192.168.1.228/api/clearScreen?screen=0

